course: dictionary
lesson: 15495
title: Studying: learning and looking closely
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Studying means spending time learning about a subject, by reading, practising or going to lessons. «Mia is studying for her spelling test tonight.» Here studying means learning the spellings so she can do well in the test.
explain: Studying can also mean looking at something carefully to understand it. «The scientist was studying a leaf under a microscope.» She is not doing a test. She is looking closely to find out how the leaf works.
explain: The words around studying give you clues. Test, subject and lessons point to learning. A map, a leaf or the stars point to looking carefully. Ask yourself: is the person learning a subject, or looking closely at something?
fact: Studying means learning about a subject by reading, practising or going to lessons.
fact: Studying can also mean looking at something carefully to understand it.
fact: «Studying for a test» means learning the things you need to know before the test.
fact: Pupils study maths, science and English at school.
fact: Scientists study animals, stars and diseases to find out how they work.
exercise: «Mia is studying for her spelling test tonight.» What does studying mean here? | Sleeping early before the test | *Learning about spelling so she can do well in the test | Eating her tea quietly | Playing games on the computer
exercise: «He was studying the map to find the way to the lake.» What was he doing? | Throwing the map away | Asking for a sandwich | Drawing a picture of a lake | *Looking at the map carefully to understand it
exercise: «Pupils are studying science and maths at school.» Which meaning of studying fits best? | Shouting loudly in the playground | *Learning about the subject through lessons and practice | Going on a holiday to the sea | Swimming in the school pool
test: «The scientist was studying the stars through a telescope all night.» What is the scientist doing? | Cooking supper | Sleeping under the stars | Buying a new telescope | *Looking closely at the stars to understand them
test: Older pupils spend evenings studying for their tests. What does studying for a test mean? | Forgetting everything before the test | Watching television until late | Writing a letter to a friend | *Learning the things needed for the test
exam: «Ravi has been studying hard at university, reading books every day.» What does studying hard mean? | Being very loud in class | Running very fast around the field | *Working very hard at learning | Sleeping in on weekends
